The '''Battle of Austerlitz''' (2 December 1805), also known as the Battle of the
Three Emperors, was one of the most important engagements of the [[Napoleonic Wars]].

== Prelude ==

Kutuzov could call upon some 110,000 men in the theatre, but the Austrian
contingents strung along the march route never reached the field.

== The battle ==

Napoleon directed the battle in person from the Zuran hill, while Marshal
Soult's corps stormed the Pratzen Heights at dawn under thick fog.

